Y</b>

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:12.180
Congratulations on being accepted here.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:14.810
Thank you very much!

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.460
Welcome to our school.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.200
How pretty!

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:32.580
<i>As of today I, Suzumi Hiyori, am a 
Sakuragaoka High School first-year!</i>

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.100
<i>My new school life...</i>

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.150
<i>starts now!</i>

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.630
So...

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.880
Where am I?!

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:48.220
How many classes are there here?! 
My middle school only had two!

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.600
I'm all turned around!

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.770
Is something wrong?

00:04:56.270 --> 00:05:01.900
Yes! I'm lost! Where are 
the first-year classrooms?!

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.970
Go down these stairs and take a left.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.200
Thank you very much!

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.200
Bye!

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.080
First-years are so young and adorable.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.440
You're not much different, Hina.

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.090
I'm not talking about looks!

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:28.330
Don't act like you're so mature just 
because you grew a few centimeters.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:29.490
She's right.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.540
Look at her, Kotaro.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:35.140
Setoguchi's the one who's 
<i>developed</i> nicely here.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:39.040
That's not what we're 
talking about, Shibaken!

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:41.890
Quiet down.

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:48.220
Anyway, I'm looking forward to seeing 
which newbies join the soccer team.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:50.100
Better make sure some first-year rookie

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.790
doesn't steal your shot 
at the starting lineup.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:06:04.670
<b>Keep quiet in the hallway</b>

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:55.450
As if I'd mess that up!

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:56.880
I have my doubts.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.550
So, Kodai!

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:03.460
Shall we go find some potential 
first-year girlfriends for you?

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:07.930
Actually, Shibaken, isn't your 
little brother a first-year?

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.680
Hmm? Oh, yeah...

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.730
<b>Welcome, Incoming Students!!</b>

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:28.020
<i>First impressions are key. 
Please don't let me screw up.</i>

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:28.610
<i>Okay!</i>

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.290
Isn't that Yujiro?

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:34.700
No way! In the flesh?!

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.700
He's even cooler in person!

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.710
Damn, he's super cute!

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:38.710
<i>What's goin' on?</i>

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:40.540
Let's go talk to him later!

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:44.880
It's you!

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.480
From yesterday, with the cops—

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:46.480
Good morning!

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.380
I look forward to our year together!

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:54.360
Aizo?! No way!

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:57.120
OMG, he's so hot!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:00.380
All right, everyone in your seats, please.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.690
Your seats are ordered 
by your student numbers.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.330
Wh-What's with him?!

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:13.160
<b><i>Suzumi</i></b>

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:13.160
Let's see, my seat is...

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:16.350
Quickly, please.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.500
Excuse me...

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.290
Don't get in my way, trash.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:27.800
That's rich, coming from you.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:30.420
<i>Uh...</i>

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.550
<i>What's...</i>

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:34.270
<i>going on here?</i>

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:38.570
I'm Akechi, your homeroom teacher. 
I teach classical literature.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:41.520
<i>Why is the literature 
teacher wearing a lab coat?</i>

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:39.710
Nice to meet you.

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:42.690
Now, everyone, introduce yourselves.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:46.070
It's nice to meet you! I'll do my best!

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.850
I'm Shibasaki Aizo. Nice to meet you!

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:52.450
Nice to meet you!

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:56.180
I'm S-Suzumi H-Hiyori!

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:04.160
I'm Someya Yujiro. Let's enjoy 
our high school lives together.

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:05.380
We will!

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:06.790
We so will!

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:10.470
<i>Uh, what's happening here?</i>

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:12.730
Nice to meet you, Suzumi-san.

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:15.740
Y-Yes, pleased to meet you!

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.420
<i>Wait, he's nice?</i>

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:21.480
<i>I thought he'd be scary.</i>

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.860
What's up with those two?

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:37.370
Aw, man, I didn't get to talk to any 
of the other girls on my first day!

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:40.160
Wait, where's the school gate?!

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:41.410
Cut the bullshit!

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:47.210
What the hell were you doing?!

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.250
None of your business, Aizo.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:50.880
Those two?

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:54.290
You think your brush with 
the law doesn't affect me?

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:55.880
It's over now.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.260
Cut the crap!

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.100
Stop! Don't fight—

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:09.150
Uh, sorry...

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:16.030
But no fightin', okay? We're all classmates.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:18.670
You might even become friends!

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:22.290
Don't you know who we are?

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:29.540
Don't <i>you</i> get in my way, 
either, you potato face!

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:32.050
<b>POTATO</b>

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.580
P-Potato?!

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:36.760
You know what to expect if you 
tell anyone about yesterday.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:40.110
This is why I hate girls.

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:41.610
Stay away from us.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.390
Wh...

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:47.450
Why?!

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:53.840
Did I do somethin' wrong?

00:09:56.140 --> 00:09:58.820
<i>It's LIP×LIP's nationwide concert tour...</i>

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:01.450
<i>The Julieta Tour you've been waiting for!</i>

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:07.770
<i>Julietas all over Japan...</i>

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:10.290
<i>We're on our way to you.</i>

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:17.410
Huh?!

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:22.970
<i>Today's guests are the super-popular 
high school idol unit...</i>

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:26.060
Tonight's Guests

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:26.060
An Idol Unit Skyrocketing in Popularity

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:26.060
<i>LIP×LIP!</i>

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:28.030
They're on TV...

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.940
<i>The studio audience is going wild!</i>

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:33.610
Tonight's Guests

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:33.610
How They Debuted

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:33.610
<i>Let's dive right in. What led to your debut?</i>

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.610
What led to your debut?

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:41.240
<b>Yujiro</b>

00:10:33.610 --> 00:11:00.340
The Two LIP×LIP Members

00:10:33.610 --> 00:11:00.340
How They Debuted

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:41.240
<b>Aizo</b>

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:38.180
<i>We auditioned. We did it separately,</i>

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:40.510
<i>but they paired us up for some reason.</i>

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:41.240
<i>Right?</i>

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:44.160
<i>Originally I was going to 
be the only one to debut,</i>

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.450
<i>but for some reason they added on Aizo.</i>

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.450
They <b>added </b>on Aizo

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:48.200
<i>I'm the add-on?!</i>

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:51.730
I'm the <b>add-on</b>

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:51.730
<i>Yeah. To put it in pass-fail terms...</i>

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.460
I guess you... <b>scraped </b>by?

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:53.960
<i>I guess you... scraped by?</i>

00:10:55.230 --> 00:11:00.340
I'm Aizo, the guy who <b>scraped </b>by!!

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.760
<i>I'm Aizo, the guy who scraped by!</i>

00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:00.340
You two are totally in sync~

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:00.340
<i>You two are totally in sync.</i>

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.900
<i>They're smilin'!</i>

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:05.600
<i>They're actin' like they get along, 
but they were glarin' hard at each other.</i>

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:07.720
<i>I don't get it.</i>

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:12.960
<i>But hey, it's none of my business. 
And they told me to stay away.</i>

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:15.740
<i>I'll try to stay away.</i>

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:16.980
Aizo!

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:18.400
Yujiro!

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:19.480
They smiled!

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.170
Gotta snap a pic!

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:21.680
Who's that girl between them?

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:22.950
She's in the way!

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.730
<i>I </i>want<i> to stay away!</i>

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:36.630
<b>School Store</b>

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:38.560
What the heck?!

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:40.760
Oh! I gotta buy somethin', too!

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:44.920
Um! I'd like some bread too, please!

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.760
<b>Bread SOLD OUT
Sorry!</b>

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:47.760
Thanks for coming by!

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:50.410
Aw, man!

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:55.810
That was a loud grumble!

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.820
Wanna have half of my sandwich?

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:01.060
What? Really?!

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:04.950
Oh, but I can't accept 
food from a stranger.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:10.360
I'm not a stranger. I'm Juri Hattori.
I'm in your class!

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:13.080
We gotta help each other out.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:16.630
Thank you! Don't mind if I do, then.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.930
E-Excuse me...

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:21.090
Is it okay if I eat with you?

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:21.990
Who're you?

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:26.600
Nakamura Chizuru. I'm in your class, too.

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:29.190
Yep! Let's eat together!

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:32.480
Here you go.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.810
Wow, it looks great!

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.330
How much was it?

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:37.800
250 yen.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:40.480
So since we're splittin' it, I owe 125.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.940
Don't sweat it. My treat.

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:44.290
That won't do.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:48.560
This stuff is more important with 
friends than with strangers.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:51.240
I respect your money, Hattori-san.

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:57.820
You can call me Juri.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.630
I'll call you Hiyori.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.480
Okay. Thanks for lunch, Juri-chan.

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:08.510
It's so good!

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:11.440
I'm not sure I've ever 
had a sandwich this good.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:14.940
Is it because I'm hungry? 
Because you split it with me?

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.850
Maybe both!

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:19.060
Anyway, it's super good!

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:23.060
That's funny! You're a character, Hiyori.

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:27.320
But you're usually all shy 
with those idols on either side.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.680
It's because of where I sit!

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:32.530
You're friends with them, 
aren't you, Suzumi-san?

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:37.330
What? No, I didn't even know they were idols.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:40.100
What was the name? Lip...

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:44.260
LIP×LIP. Any high school 
girl should know that.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.400
Really?

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:49.190
I'm not an expert, but yes,
 they're very popular.

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:52.180
They're touring the whole 
country this summer.

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:58.460
They may say "whole country," but no 
star's ever come to my little town.

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:00.690
I don't care about idols.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:07.860
But that idol smile just 
cleanses the soul, doesn't it?

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:13.120
<i>Am I the only one who 
finds those smiles scary?</i>

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:19.210
Whoa, there's so much track 
equipment! I'm impressed.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:23.820
We've got more than equipment. 
Our track team is the cream of the crop!

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:24.940
Setoguchi!

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:25.700
Yes?

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:30.060
Oh, you two know each other?

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:32.600
We met the day of the entrance ceremony.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.700
Did you make it to your classroom?

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:38.570
Yes, thank you for your help!

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:40.470
This is the new member I told you about,

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:43.470
the one who came to Tokyo to do track.

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:46.030
Oh, I've been waiting for this!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:49.420
My name's Setoguchi Hina. I'm a 
second-year. Nice to meet you!

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:52.840
I'm Suzumi Hiyori! So, um...

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:56.290
Can I run, too?!

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:00.320
So you're living alone here, huh?

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:03.790
Yeah. My town's high school 
doesn't have a track team.

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:08.470
So my teacher from middle school 
put me in touch with this school!

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:11.440
That sounds rough. Are you okay?

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:14.030
I did basic house chores there.

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:18.840
And I'm willin' to do whatever 
it takes to be on a track team!

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:21.140
My family's rootin' for me, too.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:25.050
What?! Dad hurt his back?!

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:26.780
<i>Yep.</i>

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:30.230
The doctor told him to 
stay in bed for a while.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:34.270
Idiot! As if a fisherman can just 
<i>rest</i> because of a little back strain!

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:35.020
Take that!

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:38.050
Ow! Ow, ow, stop it! Stop!

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:39.850
Get offa me!

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:41.710
I'm on the phone, guys!

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.140
<i>Be quiet!</i>

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:47.460
So he won't be able to fish for a while, huh?

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.930
<i>Can we afford Tokyo?</i>

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:54.180
No need to worry. We'll keep 
sendin' your allowance.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.430
But...

00:15:56.170 --> 00:16:00.930
The other kids just started middle school
 and elementary school, too.

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.350
That costs money.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:06.830
<i>Sure, it'll be a little tight,
 but we'll manage.</i>

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:11.700
Mom, I'm gonna get a job.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:16.580
<i>There are lots of businesses in Tokyo,
 so there's lots of places to work!</i>

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:19.780
<i>So put Minoru and the others first, okay?</i>

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:21.040
But...

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.080
<i>It'll be fine!</i>

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:26.840
I'm a high schooler now. 
Count on me for this, okay?

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:28.800
<i>Hiyori...</i>

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:32.180
<i>Thanks. That helps.</i>

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:34.280
<i>But we'll still pay your tuition, yeah?</i>

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:37.510
Yep! And I'll earn my livin' expenses!

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:42.650
Gotta look for a job...

00:16:45.550 --> 00:16:48.500
Couldn't you come a little 
earlier on weekdays?

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:51.570
I'm sorry, I have practice.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:52.740
Can you do weekends?

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:55.530
When I don't have track meets...

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:01.540
I need someone who can work 
at least four days a week.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.540
Let's just say it's not the right fit.

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:09.040
So many businesses and jobs, but none fit me.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:14.590
I need someplace with a short-term, 
low-hours job that pays well.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:15.430
Hourly rate...

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:18.310
1,500 yen?!

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:19.100
<b>1,500 per hour</b>

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:22.600
<i>"Responsibilities: helping to run events.</i>

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:25.850
<i>No experience required. Flexible hours."</i>

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:29.320
<i>And they're seekin' someone with 
motivation and physical stamina!</i>

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:32.020
<i>I have </i>so much<i> of those things!</i>

00:17:39.470 --> 00:17:42.410
<i>Are they all applyin' for the job?!</i>

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:47.110
<i>Well, that's Tokyo and a 
1,500 per hour job for ya.</i>

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:50.030
<i>But... I can't back down!</i>

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:54.880
According to our list, 
you're Suzumi Hiyori-san?

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:57.800
Y-Y-Yes! I'm pleased to meet you!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:00.680
What made you want to apply for this job?

00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:02.430
I need it to live!

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:07.180
<i>Oh, no, I messed up! I meant to 
say, "It's for living expenses"!</i>

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:11.860
We all need money to live, that's for sure.

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:14.260
I see that you don't have a work history.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:18.150
This job will be a lot of work. 
Are you sure you can handle it?

00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:20.140
There will be late nights.

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:23.540
I can do that. I'm confident that 
I've got the physical stamina.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:25.630
I won't sleep in or be late, either!

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:30.120
That's easy to say. But you've 
got school and the track team,

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.880
so your working hours will 
be limited, won't they?

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:36.510
If I'm honest, yes.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.260
However!

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:41.890
I'll get it done, no matter what.

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:44.230
I'll clear any obstacle!

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:48.180
See, on the track team, I'm a hurdler.

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:52.030
I've loved runnin' since I was a kid.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:56.690
I moved to Tokyo all alone because 
I wanted to keep runnin'.

00:18:57.020 --> 00:19:02.010
My dream is to be a national finalist.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:04.790
Having a dream is important,

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:08.830
because you can stick with it through
 the tough times if it's for your dream.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:12.900
Yes, ma'am! So I'll do whatever it takes.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:14.050
I'll work hard!

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:15.500
Suzumi-san...

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:19.470
You're a first-year at 
Sakuragaoka High School.

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:20.340
What class?

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.840
Er, Class 4.

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:24.300
Class 4...

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:28.030
One last thing.

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:31.300
Do you have any favorite pop idols?

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:34.310
Idols?

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:40.740
Absolutely not!

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:45.620
I lost the job. I just know it.

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:52.370
I made a total "blech" face. 
That's a terrible impression to make.

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:59.400
I came to Tokyo 'cause I wanted to keep 
runnin'... but is that impossible?

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:08.040
No! Hurdles exist to be cleared!

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:10.050
I'll restart my job hunt!

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:14.750
Hello?

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:20.380
Let me reintroduce myself. I'm Uchida Mayu.

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:23.030
R-Right, hello.

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:25.110
This way, please.

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:32.300
Er, did I really get the job?

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:37.250
Yes. The CEO and I discussed it,
 and we decided on you.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.020
Thank you very much!

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:44.970
Thank goodness...

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.080
Will you be able to live now?

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:48.890
Yes!

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:54.140
But there were so many applicants...
Why'd you pick me?

00:20:54.830 --> 00:21:01.400
Because you're in Sakuragaoka 
High School Class 1-4.

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:03.220
Huh?

00:21:09.170 --> 00:21:10.700
Ah, she's here.

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:18.960
Someya-kun? Shibasaki-kun?

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.660
What are <i>you</i> doing here?

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:24.270
Isn't this office authorized 
personnel only, ma'am?

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:28.970
Yes, it is. And starting today,
 she's your personnel.

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:30.400
What?

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:31.890
What does that mean?

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:36.730
I'm sure you've met in class, 
but allow me to formally introduce her.

00:21:37.110 --> 00:21:38.480
This is Hiyoko.

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:39.650
It's "Hiyori."

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:45.660
Starting today, Hiyoko the newbie will 
be LIP×LIP's manager-in-training.

00:21:45.660 --> 00:21:46.570
What?

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:47.700
What?!

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:50.950
H-Huh?

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.950
What?!

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.950
<b>Episode 1</b>

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.950
<b>I Don't Understand Idols!</b>

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:32.840
Next time, on episode 2 of 
<i>Heroines Run the Show</i>...

00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:35.180
"The Manager-in-Training Job"!

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Episode 2
The Manager-in-Training Job</b>
